+{"kind":"task","id":"ss-spec-anchor","title":"Create Speedrift spec anchor for state-system first deployment","description":"```wg-contract\nschema = 1\nmode = \"core\"\nobjective = \"Create Speedrift spec anchor for state-system first deployment\"\nnon_goals = [\n  \"No fallbacks/retries/guardrails unless acceptance requires it\",\n]\ntouch = [\n]\nacceptance = [\n]\nmax_files = 25\nmax_loc = 800\npit_stop_after = 3\nauto_followups = true\n```\n\nWrite a lightweight Speedrift drift anchor for the first deployment. Synthesize the North Star, first-deployment blueprint, source-event/idempotency contract, and system pressure test into an execution spec.\n\n## Model-Mediated Boundary\n- Code owns schemas, persistence, provenance, replay, and governance enforcement.\n- The model owns durable meaning, salience, uncertainty, memory promotion, and opportunity judgment.\n- Do not encode business judgment as static routing or action heuristics.\n\n## Pressure Test\n- Does the spec preserve source event -> trigger -> evidence -> model review -> governance -> journal/snapshot -> recent change -> package?\n- Does it distinguish Workgraph execution state from State System organizational state?\n- Does it keep Laura and Patrick as pressure-test personas without making the design SampleCo-specific?\n\n## Validation\n- [ ] Spec anchor exists at docs/specs/2026-04-28-state-system-speedrift-plan.md.\n- [ ] Spec lists implementation phases and acceptance gates.\n- [ ] Spec names the fixture traces that must pass.\n- [ ] Spec contains no temporary placeholder markers or brittle rule like deal won means post.","status":"done","priority":50,"assigned":"agent-16","before":["ss-contracts-fixtures"],"tags":["state-system","speedrift","specdrift","eval-scheduled"],"inputs":["docs/NORTH_STAR.md","docs/concepts/first-deployment-implementation-blueprint.md","docs/concepts/system-pressure-test.md"],"deliverables":["docs/specs/2026-04-28-state-system-speedrift-plan.md"],"created_at":"2026-04-28T