-{"kind":"task","id":"ss-cli","title":"Implement local CLI access surface","description":"```wg-contract\nschema = 1\nmode = \"core\"\nobjective = \"Implement local CLI access surface\"\nnon_goals = [\n  \"No fallbacks/retries/guardrails unless acceptance requires it\",\n]\ntouch = [\n]\nacceptance = [\n]\nmax_files = 25\nmax_loc = 800\npit_stop_after = 3\nauto_followups = true\n```\n\nImplement the first local CLI: state validate, state trigger, state get, state journal, state memory, state rollups, state recent, and state package. The CLI is an access adapter over existing modules.\n\n## Pressure Test\n- Can a human inspect why state changed without reading raw implementation files?\n- Can Laura and Patrick recent/package queries be reproduced from CLI?\n- Can validation run without model/API access?\n\n## Validation\n- [ ] CLI commands have tests or smoke checks.\n- [ ] CLI preserves machine-readable output where useful.\n- [ ] CLI does not duplicate store/reviewer/committer logic.","status":"done","priority":50,"before":["ss-e2e-pressure-harness"],"after":["ss-recent-context-packaging"],"tags":["state-system","cli","eval-scheduled"],"deliverables":["state_system/cli"],"created_at":"2026-04-28T21:11:37.963226+00:00","completed_at":"2026-04-30T21:06:13Z","log":[{"timestamp":"2026-04-28T21:11:37.963041+00:00","user":"braydon","message":"Task paused"},{"timestamp":"2026-04-28T21:11:53.921727+00:00","user":"braydon","message":"Task published"},{"timestamp":"2026-04-30T21:06:13Z","message":"Implemented local CLI access surface for validate, trigger, get, journal, memory, rollups, recent, and package commands. Validation: tests/test_cli.py; python3 -m state_system.cli --project-root . validate; full harness 42 tests; drifts check green."}],"context_scope":"graph"}
-{"kind":"task","id":".evaluate-ss-pressure-routing-freshness","title":"Evaluate: Pressure test routing, freshness, and package redaction","description":"```wg-contract\nschema = 1\nmode = \"core\"\nobjective = \"Evaluate: Pressure test routing, freshness, and package redaction\"\nnon_goals = [\n  \"No fallbacks/retries/guardrails unless acceptance requires it\",\n]\ntouch = [\n]\nacceptance = [\n]\nmax_files = 25\nmax_loc = 800\npit_stop_after = 3\nauto_followups = true\n```\n\n## Agent Identity\n\n### Role: Evaluator\nGrades actor-agents that have completed tasks. Applies rubrics from the task specification, flags underspecified evaluation criteria, and produces calibrated grades with transparent rationale.\n\n#### Skills\n- **cardinal-scale-grading**\nProduce a numerical score (0.0–1.0) with calibrated confidence. The primary grading modality.\ncardinal-scale-grading\n- **ordinal-scale-grading**\nRank performance relative to a reference set (other agents, historical baselines) without producing absolute scores. Useful when absolute calibration is difficult.\nordinal-scale-grading\n- **rubric-interpretation**\nParse and apply an explicit rubric provided with the task. Maps to rubric specification spectrum levels 1–4.\nrubric-interpretation\n- **domain-specific-evaluation-standards**\nApply evaluation norms from a particular field (e.g., software engineering, research, creative writing). Invoked when task rubric specifies a domain standard.\ndomain-specific-evaluation-standards\n- **underspecification-detection**\nIdentify when a task has no rubric (control by omission) and flag this before grading rather than making arbitrary meaningmaking decisions.\nunderspecification-detection\n- **grade-transparency**\nProduce grades with sufficient rationale that a human reviewer or peer evaluator can assess the grading quality. Makes the evaluator evaluable.\ngrade-transparency\n\n#### Desired Outcome\n**Calibrated evaluation grade**\nA calibrated grade (0.0–1.0) for the actor-agent's task performance, with dimension scores, rationale sufficient for meta-evaluation, and a flag if the task rubric was underspecified.\n\n**Success Criteria:**\n- Grade is calibrated and accurate\n- Dimension scores provided\n- Rationale sufficient for meta-evaluation\n\n### Operational Parameters\n#### Acceptable Trade-offs\n- Standard rubric application\n- Reasonable benefit of doubt\n\n#### Non-negotiable Constraints\n- Arbitrary grade inflation or deflation\n- Strategic grading to optimize own performance history\n\n---\n\nEvaluate the completed task 'ss-pressure-routing-freshness'.\n\nRun `wg evaluate run ss-pressure-routing-freshness` to produce a structured evaluation.\nThis reads the task output from `.workgraph/output/ss-pressure-routing-freshness/` and the task definition via `wg show ss-pressure-routing-freshness`.","status":"open","priority":10,"after":[".flip-ss-pressure-routing-freshness"],"tags":["evaluation","agency"],"exec":"wg evaluate run ss-pressure-routing-freshness","created_at":"2026-05-03T11:05:32.387872+00:00","model":"haiku","provider":"anthropic","agent":"3184716484e6f0ea08bb13539daf07686ee79d440505f1fdf2de0357707034c3","exec_mode":"bare"}
