-{"kind":"task","id":"ss-recent-context-packaging","title":"Implement recent-change registry and context packages","description":"```wg-contract\nschema = 1\nmode = \"core\"\nobjective = \"Implement recent-change registry and context packages\"\nnon_goals = [\n  \"No fallbacks/retries/guardrails unless acceptance requires it\",\n]\ntouch = [\n]\nacceptance = [\n]\nmax_files = 25\nmax_loc = 800\npit_stop_after = 3\nauto_followups = true\n```\n\nImplement recent-change indexing, persona routing metadata, routing audits, freshness metadata, excluded-context summaries, and package assembly for standing/recent/opportunity packages.\n\n## Model-Mediated Boundary\nRouting and packaging may select candidate context using explicit metadata, but must not decide salience or create actions. Laura decides whether a packaged change is a marketing opportunity.\n\n## Pressure Test\n- Laura is not flooded by low-level software tasks.\n- Laura can still see a market-facing capability when affected state refs cross into her watched domains.\n- Sensitive relationship details are redacted or summarized according to governance.\n- Stale packages cannot support external action without refresh.\n\n## Validation\n- [ ] Recent-change entries preserve source, journal, commit, routing, and freshness refs.\n- [ ] Package tests cover included, excluded, ambient, and escalated context.\n- [ ] Package freshness/watermark checks are represented.\n- [ ] No code rule says deal won means post.","status":"done","priority":50,"before":["ss-cli","ss-paia-memory-adapter","ss-pressure-routing-freshness"],"after":["ss-committer-materializer"],"tags":["state-system","recent-change","context-package","eval-scheduled"],"inputs":["docs/concepts/recent-change-registry-and-agent-opportunities.md","docs/concepts/agent-context-packages.md","docs/concepts/routing-audit-and-freshness.md"],"deliverables":["state_system/recent_changes","state_system/context_packages"],"created_at":"2026-04-28T21:11:37.950114+00:00","co