 {"kind":"task","id":"ss-source-idempotency","title":"Implement source-event ingestion and idempotency","description":"```wg-contract\nschema = 1\nmode = \"core\"\nobjective = \"Implement source-event ingestion and idempotency\"\nnon_goals = [\n  \"No fallbacks/retries/guardrails unless acceptance requires it\",\n]\ntouch = [\n]\nacceptance = [\n]\nmax_files = 25\nmax_loc = 800\npit_stop_after = 3\nauto_followups = true\n```\n\nImplement source-event ingestion for the local runner. Accept source-event envelopes, validate them, persist them, dedupe by idempotency key, and create triggers only for new events.\n\n## Model-Mediated Boundary\nSource ingestion catches facts and identity only. It must not decide marketing opportunity, project health, launch readiness, or persona salience.\n\n## Pressure Test\n- Linear webhook plus scheduled sync reports the same deal stage change. Only one downstream trigger should be created.\n- A semantically duplicate event should be flagged for review instead of blindly creating duplicate journal/recent-change/package records.\n- Partial sync evidence should carry uncertainty forward.\n\n## Validation\n- [ ] Replaying examples/source-linear-southern-abrasives-won.json is idempotent.\n- [ ] Duplicate source events do not create duplicate triggers.\n- [ ] Partial sync/confidence fields survive into evidence context.\n- [ ] No source adapter code decides action salience.","status":"done","priority":50,"before":["ss-pressure-idempotency","ss-runner-fixture-reviewer"],"after":["ss-contracts-fixtures"],"tags":["state-system","source-events","idempotency","eval-scheduled"],"inputs":["docs/concepts/source-events-and-idempotency.md","schemas/source-event.schema.json"],"deliverables":["state_system/runner"],"created_at":"2026-04-28T21:10:21.171976+00:00","completed_at":"2026-04-29T16:51:32.385723+00:00","log":[{"timestamp":"2026-04-28T21:10:21.171562+00:00","user":"braydon","message":"Task paused"},{"timestamp":"2026-04-28T21:11:53.921741+00:00"